WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.250
<i>Ollie, Ada.</i>

2
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:39.833
<i>Mom's coming.</i>

3
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:00.875
Come on, this way.

4
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:18.958
Girls!

5
00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:20.208
Mom!

6
00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:21.625
Rose!

7
00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:23.708
Mom, where are you?

8
00:01:24.666 --> 00:01:25.666
Mommy!

9
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.958
Help us! Mom!

10
00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:19.750
Dear Lord,
we ask that you keep the storms at bay.

11
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.833
Calm the dust.

12
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:25.333
We thank you for bringing Henry this job.

13
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:27.583
Preserve those who travel.

14
00:02:28.791 --> 00:02:31.875
Bring Henry in safety
to his journey's end.

15
00:02:33.208 --> 00:02:35.333
Let him earn enough to finish our home.

16
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.208
<i>Plant a crop.</i>

17
00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:39.541
<i>Help me.</i>

18
00:02:40.541 --> 00:02:44.666
<i>Help me to see the gifts you've given me
rather than the things you've taken away.</i>

19
00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:49.791
<i>Help me to keep
Rose and Ollie healthy and safe.</i>

20
00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:53.291
<i>Don't let them fall ill
like the other children.</i>

21
00:02:57.666 --> 00:03:00.875
Rose, toss down some hay, sweetheart.

22
00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:02.375
Just a little.

23
00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:05.041
We have to make it last.

24
00:03:09.541 --> 00:03:12.458
<i>Bruise me, bloody me,</i>

25
00:03:12.541 --> 00:03:15.500
<i>if it means you
won't touch a hair on their heads.</i>

26
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.125
<i>Please kiss Ada for me.</i>

27
00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:33.708
<i>Promise her that I will
fend off my human proneness</i>

28
00:03:33.791 --> 00:03:36.916
<i>for evil so that we can be together again.</i>

29
00:03:40.958 --> 00:03:42.208
<i>All of us.</i>

30
00:03:50.041 --> 00:03:53.875
{\an8}<i>And when I lie awake tonight,</i>
<i>banish worry from my heart.</i>

31
00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:58.333
<i>Reward me with peaceful black sleep.</i>

32
00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:02.208
Amen.

33
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.458
I asked your daddy to patch this.

34
00:04:05.541 --> 00:04:07.208
There's just never enough time.

35
00:04:11.041 --> 00:04:13.166
You think he'll see Philadelphia?

36
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:18.041
No, it's too far east.

37
00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:21.583
Well, I wanna see it.

38
00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:22.791
Hmm.

39
00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:24.500
I wanna see what it's like.

40
00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:28.333
Maybe next summer.

41
00:04:30.375 --> 00:04:31.958
If the crops come in.

42
00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:35.833
Lock this behind me.

43
00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:54.666
Follow my finger as I read, okay?

44
00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:02.708
"The Grey Man locked his lovely wife"

45
00:05:02.791 --> 00:05:06.666
and five children in the bedroom,
then gathered embers from the fire.

46
00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:11.833
He aimed to burn the six angels up,
but fate had one more victim in mind.

47
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.458
As the flames leaped higher,

48
00:05:14.958 --> 00:05:17.416
the Grey Man
realized his shirt was caught.

49
00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:19.291
It was no use.

50
00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:21.208
The flames consumed him.

51
00:05:22.375 --> 00:05:26.541
Now, during a dust storm,
the Grey Man's ashes blow together.

52
00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:27.708
He walks the night.

53
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:31.583
If you don't wear your mask,
you'll breathe him in,

54
00:05:31.666 --> 00:05:33.750
"and he'll make you do terrible things."

55
00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:23.625
You could come with me.

56
00:06:29.208 --> 00:06:32.875
I won't put them in a tent,
lose what little we have.

57
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
And I won't leave her out there.

58
00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.250
Alone.

59
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.083
Girl...

60
00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:47.791
So, how'd
Henry get off last week?

61
00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:49.625
- Well…
- Yeah?

62
00:07:49.708 --> 00:07:51.291
There were quite a few heading out.

63
00:07:53.666 --> 00:07:55.041
Last man standing.

64
00:07:57.708 --> 00:07:59.668
- Oh, I'm so sorry.
- That's all right.

65
00:07:59.708 --> 00:08:01.958
Just... It's hard to keep up with.

66
00:08:08.625 --> 00:08:10.333
He's been at that all night.

67
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:12.791
Is it that cold that was going around?

68
00:08:12.875 --> 00:08:15.625
It started out like that,
but it's just... it's just gotten worse.

69
00:08:15.708 --> 00:08:17.625
It's pneumonia, Dr. Cox says.

70
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:21.445
Oh, it's not catching.

71
00:08:21.958 --> 00:08:24.250
Doctor says it's
just too much dust in the air.

72
00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.333
What are we meant to do about that?

73
00:08:29.916 --> 00:08:30.958
It's a battle.

74
00:09:31.916 --> 00:09:33.625
Thomas has been poorly.

75
00:09:33.708 --> 00:09:36.517
Well, they should go see
that faith healer over in Guymon.

76
00:09:36.541 --> 00:09:39.958
He pulled the arthritis
right out of an old man's fingers.

77
00:09:40.041 --> 00:09:42.166
Bones just straightened right out.

78
00:09:44.625 --> 00:09:47.083
It's good you brought the girls, Margaret.

79
00:09:50.666 --> 00:09:51.916
Why is that?

80
00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:56.625
I guess you haven't heard about Calabash.

81
00:09:56.708 --> 00:09:58.333
The daddy said the door was locked.

82
00:09:58.416 --> 00:10:00.875
But the drifter
got into the house somehow.

83
00:10:00.958 --> 00:10:02.166
Ransacked the pantry.

84
00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.934
They found him
eating crackers over the baby.

85
00:10:03.958 --> 00:10:06.291
No, Birdie,
he'd already finished the crackers.

86
00:10:06.375 --> 00:10:08.375
He was just looking at the baby.

87
00:10:08.458 --> 00:10:09.767
He must have been hungry.

88
00:10:09.791 --> 00:10:12.500
Hunger don't explain
staring at a baby like that.

89
00:10:12.583 --> 00:10:13.458
Just staring.

90
00:10:13.541 --> 00:10:16.791
And it certainly don't
explain what he did after.

91
00:10:20.333 --> 00:10:22.000
He tied the daddy up

92
00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:26.416
and made him watch
while he killed the mama and the kids.

93
00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.958
Gutted like hogs.

94
00:10:29.166 --> 00:10:31.000
Can't keep up with chores as it is.

95
00:10:31.541 --> 00:10:33.666
How am I supposed
to watch out for fiends too?

96
00:10:35.083 --> 00:10:36.250
You keep your guard up.

97
00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:37.750
Always.

98
00:10:38.666 --> 00:10:40.226
Did they ever catch him?

99
00:10:40.458 --> 00:10:41.458
The drifter.

100
00:10:42.041 --> 00:10:43.083
No, not yet.

101
00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:44.625
And I can't figure it.

102
00:10:44.708 --> 00:10:46.833
Nobody saw him leave.

103
00:10:46.916 --> 00:10:50.375
It's like he just melted into the dust.

104
00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.625
Oh, sweet Jesus.

105
00:10:58.541 --> 00:11:00.291
Goodness.

106
00:11:17.291 --> 00:11:19.250
You're not leaving today.

107
00:11:19.333 --> 00:11:20.333
Trying to.

108
00:11:20.416 --> 00:11:22.642
The wind is terrible.
There must be a storm coming.

109
00:11:22.666 --> 00:11:23.809
There's always a storm coming.

110
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:26.833
But people die in them and
you'll be exposed on that cart, Esther.

111
00:11:26.916 --> 00:11:28.000
Unprotected.

112
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.458
All you need to do is make sure
Thomas and Jacob stay inside.

113
00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:36.333
Clean. Seal the house.

114
00:11:36.416 --> 00:11:38.500
Even so,
it seeps through everything.

115
00:11:38.583 --> 00:11:40.666
Keep finding it in the oddest places.

116
00:11:43.375 --> 00:11:46.833
I had a dream last night that, um...

117
00:11:47.791 --> 00:11:50.583
He would not stop coughing.

118
00:11:52.958 --> 00:11:56.958
I took a handkerchief,
and I stuffed it in his mouth.

119
00:11:57.666 --> 00:12:01.083
Over and over and over.

120
00:12:08.458 --> 00:12:09.625
Sorry.

121
00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:13.541
I just got to get my boys outta here.

122
00:12:28.583 --> 00:12:30.916
Whoa. Easy. Easy.

123
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.958
Girls, grab the twine
or you'll get lost in the dust!

124
00:13:15.708 --> 00:13:16.916
Where's Ollie?

125
00:13:17.416 --> 00:13:18.541
I can't see her.

126
00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.625
What man?

127
00:14:33.125 --> 00:14:34.208
Stay here.

128
00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.750
Mom, don't go out there.

129
00:15:04.791 --> 00:15:06.166
The Grey Man?

130
00:15:07.166 --> 00:15:08.875
You scared her with this, Rose.

131
00:15:10.916 --> 00:15:13.041
Didn't I tell you to get rid of this?

132
00:15:13.125 --> 00:15:14.166
Yeah.

133
00:15:18.125 --> 00:15:20.541
This should help with the dust, okay?

134
00:15:24.125 --> 00:15:25.375
What about that man?

135
00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.583
That drifter that disappeared.

136
00:15:30.666 --> 00:15:32.333
There isn't anyone out there.

137
00:15:32.833 --> 00:15:34.083
Understand?

138
00:15:54.166 --> 00:15:55.208
I'm taking this.

139
00:16:04.166 --> 00:16:05.666
Will you tell us about the wheat?

140
00:16:18.291 --> 00:16:20.833
The first year we planted,
it just took hold.

141
00:16:29.833 --> 00:16:34.541
When the wind blew,
the weeds would wave like the ocean.

142
00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:44.208
And one day, we played hide-and-seek
in the tall grass for hours.

143
00:16:46.875 --> 00:16:47.875
Come on.

144
00:16:48.666 --> 00:16:50.291
Hurry up.

145
00:16:50.375 --> 00:16:54.083
<i>You could hide
inches away, and I couldn't see you.</i>

146
00:16:55.875 --> 00:16:57.958
<i>But I could
always hear you giggling.</i>

147
00:17:00.875 --> 00:17:02.208
<i>It was perfect.</i>

148
00:17:11.958 --> 00:17:12.958
Good night.

149
00:17:48.916 --> 00:17:50.416
Mom, wake up!

150
00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.541
What? What happened?

151
00:17:53.125 --> 00:17:55.333
Ollie was right.
Someone's outside.

152
00:18:02.625 --> 00:18:03.625
See?

153
00:18:33.333 --> 00:18:34.333
Wait here.

154
00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.750
It's Jacob.

155
00:20:33.708 --> 00:20:35.000
Esther's boy.

156
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.601
Cart must have gotten
overturned in the storm last night.

157
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:43.916
Where's Esther?

158
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.000
I don't know.

159
00:20:46.166 --> 00:20:48.208
I found Thomas
hiding under the cart alone,

160
00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.000
so scared I could barely
get him to come out.

161
00:20:51.916 --> 00:20:54.500
Probably left him there when
she went to go look for Jacob.

162
00:21:40.791 --> 00:21:42.916
The Lord
works in mysterious ways.

163
00:21:49.875 --> 00:21:51.500
But he's a wise provider.

164
00:21:52.666 --> 00:21:55.458
All you can do is hold faith.

165
00:21:55.541 --> 00:21:58.083
Faith that He has a plan for Jacob.

166
00:21:58.875 --> 00:22:02.625
A plan more important
than we may ever understand.

167
00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:07.333
I guess some things…
…are just out of our hands.

168
00:22:07.416 --> 00:22:08.791
Some things aren't.

169
00:22:11.291 --> 00:22:14.125
You can't just have faith
that He'll do something,

170
00:22:14.791 --> 00:22:17.000
that it's part of the plan or they'll die.

171
00:22:17.666 --> 00:22:18.958
We'll all be buried.

172
00:22:19.041 --> 00:22:20.708
Sounds like pride to me.

173
00:22:21.708 --> 00:22:23.458
Better than burying another child.

174
00:22:24.166 --> 00:22:25.666
I tried to leave.

175
00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:26.750
In a storm.

176
00:22:27.583 --> 00:22:29.351
I can't change the weather, Margaret.

177
00:22:29.375 --> 00:22:30.708
I can't make it rain.

178
00:22:31.208 --> 00:22:32.750
What should I do?

179
00:22:32.833 --> 00:22:33.916
You might try sweeping.

180
00:23:33.583 --> 00:23:35.083
Fit as a couple of fiddles.

181
00:23:36.875 --> 00:23:38.458
It just started bleeding.

182
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.291
It wouldn't stop.

183
00:23:41.125 --> 00:23:43.333
Well, air is dry.

184
00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:45.125
That'd be my guess.

185
00:23:46.250 --> 00:23:47.375
Your guess?

186
00:23:54.791 --> 00:23:57.833
After Ollie and Ada, I just...

187
00:23:58.416 --> 00:23:59.416
I worry.

188
00:24:00.166 --> 00:24:02.583
Ada used to have
nosebleeds just like this.

189
00:24:02.666 --> 00:24:03.666
Hmm.

190
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Esther mentioned something
about the dust making Thomas ill.

191
00:24:11.875 --> 00:24:12.875
The air.

192
00:24:16.625 --> 00:24:20.000
I got some masks for sale.

193
00:24:23.166 --> 00:24:24.416
Might help.

194
00:24:27.541 --> 00:24:29.125
You're taking your sleeping aid?

195
00:24:29.208 --> 00:24:30.583
Mm-hmm.

196
00:24:30.666 --> 00:24:32.017
Well, you want my advice?

197
00:24:32.041 --> 00:24:36.000
I say keep the house sealed
best you can, wear the masks.

198
00:24:37.291 --> 00:24:38.333
Relax.

199
00:24:57.458 --> 00:24:59.208
Mom, are you awake?

200
00:25:11.166 --> 00:25:13.958
We're not even supposed to
sleep in the same room as you.

201
00:25:14.041 --> 00:25:16.500
There was only enough fabric
to seal one room.

202
00:25:19.125 --> 00:25:22.125
What if it happens again?
What if you stop sleeping?

203
00:25:26.458 --> 00:25:29.583
Don't you understand that
the dust seeps through every opening?

204
00:25:30.208 --> 00:25:34.541
That's why your cousin, Thomas, is sick
and it's why your nose is bleeding.

205
00:25:35.083 --> 00:25:38.791
Well, I want to leave.
I want to go to Dad.

206
00:25:40.083 --> 00:25:42.958
Well, when your father sends more money,
we'll take the next train.

207
00:25:44.333 --> 00:25:45.333
I promise.

208
00:26:07.333 --> 00:26:08.916
Has anyone had any mail?

209
00:26:09.875 --> 00:26:12.583
We're going to try to leave
when Henry's next letter arrives.

210
00:26:14.833 --> 00:26:19.416
Well, I guess you hadn't heard.
Service has been halted indefinitely.

211
00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:24.166
Dust built up so much, a train in Woodward
skipped plumb off the tracks.

212
00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:28.791
Killed every soul on board except for
one donkey in the freight car.

213
00:26:28.875 --> 00:26:31.416
You're stuck with us, looks like.

214
00:26:33.708 --> 00:26:34.708
I see.

215
00:26:44.250 --> 00:26:45.833
Any word on that drifter?

216
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:52.708
Well, now they're wondering
if the daddy did it himself.

217
00:26:53.708 --> 00:26:57.166
Killed those kids and made up
the intruder wholesale.

218
00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:01.333
Our neighbor said he'd been
acting off right before,

219
00:27:02.916 --> 00:27:05.041
<i>like a different man entirely.</i>

220
00:27:06.375 --> 00:27:07.458
<i>Think about it.</i>

221
00:27:08.875 --> 00:27:12.250
<i>No one saw that drifter coming or going.</i>

222
00:27:47.625 --> 00:27:49.125
Put your nightgown on, sweetheart.

223
00:28:48.333 --> 00:28:50.166
- Didn't I ask you to tie the doors?
- I did.

224
00:28:50.250 --> 00:28:52.083
That cow is keeping us alive.

225
00:28:52.166 --> 00:28:54.666
She's already starving
and something could have gotten to her.

226
00:28:54.750 --> 00:28:56.226
- She could have died.
- I tied it.

227
00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:57.770
Well, then it has to be tighter. What?

228
00:28:59.541 --> 00:29:00.416
Stop.

229
00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:03.666
No more Grey Man, understand?

230
00:29:11.916 --> 00:29:13.333
You need to finish your chores.

231
00:29:43.416 --> 00:29:44.416
Rose.

232
00:29:46.583 --> 00:29:48.375
Toss down some hay, would you?

233
00:29:59.041 --> 00:30:00.708
I'm sorry we argued, but...

234
00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:43.833
Rose!

235
00:30:49.416 --> 00:30:51.666
{\an8}In the barn, who did you see?

236
00:31:03.458 --> 00:31:05.166
But I thought you said he wasn't real.

237
00:31:06.125 --> 00:31:07.666
That doesn't mean no one's out th...

238
00:31:14.583 --> 00:31:15.583
Stay.

239
00:31:26.791 --> 00:31:31.458
Come out or I will burn this whole thing
to the ground, I swear to God.

240
00:31:51.625 --> 00:31:53.708
I told you to stay downstairs.

241
00:31:54.291 --> 00:31:55.708
We're scared.

242
00:32:07.125 --> 00:32:08.416
Stay back, girls.

243
00:32:21.375 --> 00:32:22.375
Who are you?

244
00:32:24.958 --> 00:32:26.583
Name's Brother Wallace Grady.

245
00:32:28.916 --> 00:32:30.250
I mean you no harm, ma'am.

246
00:32:31.958 --> 00:32:32.958
Just needed shelter.

247
00:32:34.416 --> 00:32:36.458
Henry told me y'all had this barn.

248
00:32:36.541 --> 00:32:38.625
Henry?

249
00:32:38.708 --> 00:32:40.583
Don't you recognize his jacket?

250
00:32:42.166 --> 00:32:43.166
Did you hurt him?

251
00:32:43.958 --> 00:32:47.000
Of course not, ma'am.
I'm a man of the cloth.

252
00:32:48.708 --> 00:32:52.708
I, uh, stopped through the works detail
on my way west

253
00:32:52.791 --> 00:32:55.416
and, Brother Henry, he give me this,

254
00:32:56.958 --> 00:32:59.000
and he asked me to check in on y'all.

255
00:32:59.916 --> 00:33:01.750
Why not just knock on the door?

256
00:33:01.833 --> 00:33:05.916
That was my intention, ma'am,
soon as I had a chance to recover.

257
00:33:06.833 --> 00:33:11.041
See, I got caught in that storm
on account of my bad leg.

258
00:33:12.583 --> 00:33:13.708
Thought I looked too poorly.

259
00:33:13.791 --> 00:33:17.125
I didn't want to scare your girls,
uh, scare you.

260
00:33:19.166 --> 00:33:20.166
Rose, right?

261
00:33:21.375 --> 00:33:23.458
And you're Margaret.

262
00:33:29.458 --> 00:33:30.875
Henry would have told me.

263
00:33:32.333 --> 00:33:34.500
The mail is slow going
with the trains out.

264
00:33:38.250 --> 00:33:41.541
You have to go. Now.

265
00:33:41.625 --> 00:33:45.875
I could earn my keep.
People need the Word of God these days.

266
00:33:45.958 --> 00:33:48.625
- People need rain.
- One follows the other, ma'am.

267
00:33:48.708 --> 00:33:51.416
Just get out! Out!

268
00:33:56.000 --> 00:34:00.875
It's just your cow's starving,
which means you're about to be.

269
00:34:02.083 --> 00:34:03.333
Right?

270
00:34:05.416 --> 00:34:08.125
The milk's dried up.
I could get her producing again.

271
00:34:09.541 --> 00:34:12.208
- Okay. It's okay, it's okay.
- Oh, darlin'.

272
00:34:12.291 --> 00:34:14.541
You're okay.

273
00:34:15.958 --> 00:34:16.958
Mom, help.

274
00:34:17.041 --> 00:34:18.791
Breathe. Breathe.

275
00:34:19.375 --> 00:34:20.458
Stay back.

276
00:34:20.541 --> 00:34:23.791
- Ma'am, I can help…
- Mom.

277
00:34:24.291 --> 00:34:25.875
…but I'd have to touch her.

278
00:34:25.958 --> 00:34:27.000
Why?

279
00:34:27.875 --> 00:34:29.875
I lay hands.

280
00:34:30.375 --> 00:34:33.333
I can heal. Truly.

281
00:34:34.291 --> 00:34:36.291
Even if you don't believe,
what could it hurt?

282
00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:42.500
Margaret.

283
00:35:14.708 --> 00:35:16.125
Mom, help!

284
00:35:16.208 --> 00:35:17.333
Let her go.

285
00:35:20.583 --> 00:35:21.666
Let her go!

286
00:35:27.625 --> 00:35:29.865
What did you do to her?

287
00:35:33.458 --> 00:35:34.458
Mom.

288
00:35:36.208 --> 00:35:37.208
It stopped.

289
00:35:49.375 --> 00:35:51.833
I'll go. I'll go.

290
00:35:53.125 --> 00:35:54.291
I just gotta rest.

291
00:35:58.958 --> 00:36:01.250
You said you could get our cow producing.

292
00:36:03.291 --> 00:36:04.291
How?

293
00:36:17.625 --> 00:36:21.291
Tumbleweeds will soak this water right up.
Yield a lot of feed.

294
00:36:32.625 --> 00:36:36.333
I sleep with this,
and I know how to use it.

295
00:36:37.708 --> 00:36:38.708
Do you understand?

296
00:36:46.625 --> 00:36:49.750
People will talk if I let you stay.

297
00:36:52.166 --> 00:36:53.958
I could keep out of sight for a bit.

298
00:36:55.291 --> 00:36:56.291
Stick to the barn.

299
00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:18.291
Did he heal me?

300
00:37:21.375 --> 00:37:22.375
I don't know.

301
00:37:46.750 --> 00:37:48.375
Rose!

302
00:39:05.083 --> 00:39:06.666
Well, I hate you, Margaret.

303
00:39:08.125 --> 00:39:09.165
What a fine hand you have.

304
00:39:10.833 --> 00:39:15.458
Oh.
It's just our dream for the house.

305
00:39:18.916 --> 00:39:21.000
Missed you in church this week, Margaret.

306
00:39:21.875 --> 00:39:23.583
We were worried about you.

307
00:39:26.375 --> 00:39:28.916
Mom, it's Thomas.

308
00:39:34.791 --> 00:39:38.416
Where's Esther?
How did he get here by himself?

309
00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:39.500
Oh, poor thing.

310
00:39:39.583 --> 00:39:41.583
Birdie, go fetch the sheriff.

311
00:39:42.083 --> 00:39:43.458
This is heartbreaking.

312
00:39:45.958 --> 00:39:48.041
She's not looking after him, Margaret.

313
00:39:48.750 --> 00:39:51.958
Maybe find out if it's
a short-term grief kind of aberration

314
00:39:52.041 --> 00:39:53.250
or something more serious.

315
00:40:03.458 --> 00:40:07.000
Esther. It's Margaret.

316
00:40:10.750 --> 00:40:12.000
Esther?

317
00:40:25.500 --> 00:40:27.333
Remember when Ada passed?

318
00:40:31.041 --> 00:40:34.000
For a long while,
I thought I might just join her.

319
00:40:36.208 --> 00:40:39.083
But you have to think of your other child.

320
00:40:39.583 --> 00:40:40.583
His health.

321
00:40:44.666 --> 00:40:49.166
The man has… been looking after him.

322
00:40:54.416 --> 00:40:55.625
Or was that a dream?

323
00:41:09.708 --> 00:41:10.708
Have some water.

324
00:41:11.833 --> 00:41:12.833
Just a sip.

325
00:41:18.166 --> 00:41:20.083
How long have you been lying here?

326
00:41:34.083 --> 00:41:37.291
She... She's not fit.

327
00:41:37.875 --> 00:41:39.083
You sure?

328
00:41:39.166 --> 00:41:42.125
I'd take him,
but we can't feed him.

329
00:41:43.666 --> 00:41:45.833
Come with me, little Thomas.
Yeah.

330
00:41:50.166 --> 00:41:52.708
Margaret.

331
00:41:52.791 --> 00:41:56.583
Thank you.
Thank you for visiting me.

332
00:41:59.375 --> 00:42:02.583
It's all right.
You just have to take care of yourself.

333
00:42:03.208 --> 00:42:05.083
What's going on?

334
00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.680
Just for a little while, Esther.

335
00:42:08.250 --> 00:42:09.750
What's for a little while?

336
00:42:11.041 --> 00:42:13.000
Just until you get back on your feet.

337
00:42:16.125 --> 00:42:19.666
Are you taking him? Where you taking him?

338
00:42:21.750 --> 00:42:24.333
I won't... Oh. Hey.
Let's just take a moment here.

339
00:42:26.708 --> 00:42:30.041
He's my son. He's all I've got left.

340
00:42:30.125 --> 00:42:32.958
You're no different than me,
you know. You know that?

341
00:42:33.916 --> 00:42:37.125
You're no different than me.
You always thought you were.

342
00:42:39.291 --> 00:42:42.166
You'll be just like me, you hear me?

343
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:43.708
I'll show you what it's like.

344
00:42:43.791 --> 00:42:47.125
Look at me. You'll be just like me.

345
00:42:47.708 --> 00:42:48.875
You see me?

346
00:42:48.958 --> 00:42:52.666
You'll be just like me.
You'll see. You'll be sorry.

347
00:42:52.750 --> 00:42:54.583
Don't take him from me.

348
00:43:06.125 --> 00:43:09.291
<i>"Count it all joy
when you fall into various trials,</i>

349
00:43:09.875 --> 00:43:13.541
knowing that the testing of your faith
produces patience."

350
00:43:18.166 --> 00:43:19.208
It's lovely.

351
00:43:20.333 --> 00:43:21.375
Yours?

352
00:43:21.458 --> 00:43:22.666
It was my mother's.

353
00:43:22.750 --> 00:43:23.750
Hmm.

354
00:43:26.875 --> 00:43:28.791
Is she how you got into the church?

355
00:43:29.791 --> 00:43:30.791
Partly.

356
00:43:31.583 --> 00:43:35.333
My daddy was a preacher.
He told me I had the touch young.

357
00:43:36.208 --> 00:43:39.625
All my siblings do. I have four sisters.

358
00:43:41.416 --> 00:43:42.416
Where are they now?

359
00:43:44.208 --> 00:43:48.166
Two are in Texas
and, uh, scarlet fever took the others

360
00:43:48.250 --> 00:43:49.833
while I was off spreading the Word.

361
00:44:10.500 --> 00:44:14.916
Ollie had it. Scarlet fever. And Ada.

362
00:44:20.208 --> 00:44:23.666
When they went into quarantine,
Ada never stopped calling out for me.

363
00:44:27.750 --> 00:44:33.958
I clawed the door separating us until
my nails were ripped away from the quick.

364
00:44:34.458 --> 00:44:37.208
Temporary parting is a burden
of our earthly lives.

365
00:44:38.916 --> 00:44:42.791
But there's a reunion
that lasts an eternity.

366
00:44:45.291 --> 00:44:46.291
You believe that?

367
00:44:47.041 --> 00:44:48.291
I have to.

368
00:44:50.875 --> 00:44:51.958
Don't have a choice.

369
00:44:54.833 --> 00:44:56.416
Those girls are lucky to have you.

370
00:45:05.041 --> 00:45:06.041
You don't think that?

371
00:45:13.916 --> 00:45:19.833
After Ada, my sleep was fitful.

372
00:45:22.583 --> 00:45:26.333
And I... I'd do things.

373
00:45:30.666 --> 00:45:35.000
No mail today. But the letter carrier said
a haze is dropping in.

374
00:45:46.750 --> 00:45:49.958
God above, I thank you.

375
00:45:51.083 --> 00:45:53.458
I thank you for the warmth
of the Bellum family.

376
00:45:54.750 --> 00:45:58.333
You connected us through Brother Henry,
and for that, I am eternally grateful.

377
00:46:00.583 --> 00:46:02.625
Thank you for Rose's continued health,

378
00:46:03.708 --> 00:46:07.791
and we ask that you hold little Ollie
in your ever-loving light.

379
00:46:10.416 --> 00:46:12.833
I'm reminded of a verse
that my father taught me.

380
00:46:14.333 --> 00:46:16.666
"Neither this man nor his parents sinned,

381
00:46:17.333 --> 00:46:22.291
but this happened so that the works of God
might be displayed in Him."

382
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:25.916
Thank you for this nourishment.

383
00:46:26.000 --> 00:46:29.125
And thank you for this.

384
00:46:29.208 --> 00:46:30.291
This came today?

385
00:46:30.375 --> 00:46:32.666
- Ooh, is that from Daddy?
- Mm-hmm.

386
00:46:32.750 --> 00:46:34.684
- Mm-mmm. Next one, little...
- What's he got to say?

387
00:46:34.708 --> 00:46:35.583
Stop!

388
00:46:35.666 --> 00:46:37.000
- Rose.
- Well, I...

389
00:46:42.416 --> 00:46:43.416
Hey.

390
00:46:52.166 --> 00:46:53.250
"Dear girls,"

391
00:46:54.375 --> 00:47:00.500
"my first hope is that
you can... d... deci..."

392
00:47:01.541 --> 00:47:02.541
Decipher.

393
00:47:03.166 --> 00:47:04.708
- Decipher.
- Mm-hmm.

394
00:47:05.541 --> 00:47:07.791
"Decipher my chicken scratch."

395
00:47:08.333 --> 00:47:12.458
"My second hope is that these
blades of grass will still be green

396
00:47:12.541 --> 00:47:14.434
- "by the time they reach you."
- Mmm.

397
00:47:14.458 --> 00:47:16.101
"Just know that when I picked them",

398
00:47:16.125 --> 00:47:18.500
"they were the brightest thing
you ever saw."

399
00:47:19.875 --> 00:47:22.208
"This next bit's just for Mama, girls."

400
00:47:22.291 --> 00:47:23.291
Oh.

401
00:47:24.250 --> 00:47:26.500
Come on.

402
00:47:50.125 --> 00:47:51.791
Y'all telling secrets over there?

403
00:47:54.958 --> 00:47:55.958
Now, Rose.

404
00:47:58.625 --> 00:47:59.708
Put her down.

405
00:48:03.333 --> 00:48:05.041
That seems like a bad idea.

406
00:48:05.541 --> 00:48:06.958
Who are you?

407
00:48:07.541 --> 00:48:09.916
Rose, read the letter. Aloud.

408
00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:13.958
"I'm fine, Margaret,
but my jacket was took."

409
00:48:14.041 --> 00:48:18.625
Along with the letter in its pocket,
money, and sweets for the girls.

410
00:48:18.708 --> 00:48:22.000
There was a preacher hanging about,
asked to stay the night.

411
00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:25.541
Next day, my bunkmate didn't
come back from lunch.

412
00:48:26.833 --> 00:48:31.916
Found him with his head cracked open
like an egg, boots pulled off his feet.

413
00:48:32.875 --> 00:48:36.750
"Nobody knows how the preacher made off.
Like he just vanished."

414
00:48:41.916 --> 00:48:43.125
I wouldn't have hurt y'all.

415
00:48:44.541 --> 00:48:46.166
- Where's the money?
- Gone.

416
00:48:47.291 --> 00:48:48.500
Where's yours?

417
00:48:48.583 --> 00:48:50.458
Gone. Let her go.

418
00:48:51.791 --> 00:48:54.625
I will. In exchange for that letter.

419
00:48:55.750 --> 00:48:58.291
We better hold on to it.

420
00:48:58.375 --> 00:48:59.666
See what the sheriff thinks.

421
00:49:22.958 --> 00:49:24.375
Y'all would've starved without me.

422
00:49:24.458 --> 00:49:27.750
Without you, his first letter
would have gotten to us.

423
00:49:27.833 --> 00:49:29.291
We could have left!

424
00:49:29.375 --> 00:49:31.875
"Do not neglect
to show hospitality to strangers",

425
00:49:31.958 --> 00:49:34.250
for thereby some have
entertained angels, unaware."

426
00:49:34.333 --> 00:49:36.583
- Angels.
- I fixed her, didn't I?

427
00:49:36.666 --> 00:49:38.083
How about I undo it?

428
00:49:39.458 --> 00:49:40.958
Put her back the way she was.

429
00:49:41.041 --> 00:49:44.458
Fixed her? You're a con.

430
00:49:45.708 --> 00:49:48.166
Your father, the preacher, a con too?

431
00:49:48.791 --> 00:49:51.791
My father, he'd like you.

432
00:49:54.625 --> 00:49:55.916
Get out.

433
00:50:01.458 --> 00:50:02.750
Get out!

434
00:50:16.791 --> 00:50:18.166
I'd be scared too.

435
00:50:20.750 --> 00:50:22.541
You're out here all alone.

436
00:50:25.666 --> 00:50:29.333
Don't know when a man could come by.

437
00:50:33.083 --> 00:50:35.250
A few locks. Some twine?

438
00:50:37.125 --> 00:50:40.083
That's not gonna stop me.

439
00:50:41.500 --> 00:50:43.250
That's not gonna stop the Grey Man.

440
00:50:59.250 --> 00:51:00.333
I'll be seeing y'all.

441
00:53:01.416 --> 00:53:02.416
Mommy.

442
00:53:15.250 --> 00:53:16.250
Ollie.

443
00:53:18.541 --> 00:53:19.833
Did you say that?

444
00:53:37.708 --> 00:53:39.125
What are you doing, Esther?

445
00:53:40.375 --> 00:53:42.750
You'll be just like me.

446
00:53:43.833 --> 00:53:50.625
You'll see. You'll breathe him in. He'll
make you do terrible things.

447
00:53:59.375 --> 00:54:02.333
Mama. Mama. Mama.

448
00:54:08.625 --> 00:54:10.125
Were you outside all night?

449
00:55:29.208 --> 00:55:30.750
<i>Margaret.</i>

450
00:55:32.041 --> 00:55:33.250
<i>It's not gonna stop.</i>

451
00:55:59.125 --> 00:56:01.875
Mom! Get us out!

452
00:56:01.958 --> 00:56:07.208
Mom! Mommy! Mom!

453
00:56:07.291 --> 00:56:10.875
Open the door! Unlock it, please!

454
00:56:10.958 --> 00:56:12.875
- Mom!
- Is he in there?

455
00:56:12.958 --> 00:56:14.458
Get us out!

456
00:56:19.416 --> 00:56:20.916
Mommy!

457
00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:23.666
Get out of here! Go!

458
00:56:42.083 --> 00:56:43.708
Did you knock the lamp over?

459
00:56:44.875 --> 00:56:47.041
No, it's Wallace.

460
00:56:47.125 --> 00:56:48.500
How's he doing it?

461
00:56:50.333 --> 00:56:51.833
I was up the whole night.

462
00:56:56.333 --> 00:56:57.750
And the doors are still locked.

463
00:56:59.666 --> 00:57:01.666
Unless he doesn't have to use doors.

464
00:57:01.750 --> 00:57:02.791
Mom, what do you mean?

465
00:57:07.416 --> 00:57:11.000
I should have sealed under this door.

466
00:57:13.875 --> 00:57:18.458
Mom. But the... the Grey Man's
just a story, like... like you said.

467
00:57:19.208 --> 00:57:21.166
I-I lent Wallace the book one day.

468
00:57:32.458 --> 00:57:33.750
But he healed you,

469
00:57:35.166 --> 00:57:36.166
right?

470
00:57:37.958 --> 00:57:42.291
And he came into a locked house
while I stood watch.

471
00:57:46.916 --> 00:57:48.316
That is what he wants.

472
00:57:49.625 --> 00:57:51.333
Go get your sister.

473
00:57:52.083 --> 00:57:56.750
Slide fabric under the door
and don't come out.

474
00:58:04.250 --> 00:58:05.250
Hi.

475
00:58:06.625 --> 00:58:07.875
You're looking well.

476
00:58:09.500 --> 00:58:10.666
What are you doing here?

477
00:58:12.125 --> 00:58:14.541
I've come to apologize, Margaret.

478
00:58:15.833 --> 00:58:21.875
The things that I was thinking and…
…the things I said, I'm sorry.

479
00:58:21.958 --> 00:58:23.083
We're family.

480
00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:26.625
Can't we put this all behind us
and just start fresh? I miss you.

481
00:58:26.708 --> 00:58:28.583
I miss the girls and...

482
00:58:29.625 --> 00:58:31.041
Well, you know…

483
00:58:33.083 --> 00:58:34.583
folks are starting to worry.

484
00:58:35.416 --> 00:58:38.208
They haven't seen you in a while.

485
00:58:52.125 --> 00:58:55.833
It's difficult with such low light.

486
00:58:57.416 --> 00:58:59.000
It's much easier to breathe though.

487
00:59:05.375 --> 00:59:09.125
I wonder if it might help to get out more.

488
00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:14.375
It's wild what happens upstairs
when you're allowed to stew.

489
00:59:14.458 --> 00:59:17.583
It might be good to take the lid off
and let some of that steam out.

490
00:59:18.708 --> 00:59:20.548
You know,
I've been trying to get out more too.

491
00:59:20.583 --> 00:59:23.250
I've been working with the preacher,
praying to get my head right.

492
00:59:24.208 --> 00:59:26.208
I've been visiting Thomas…

493
00:59:30.583 --> 00:59:31.625
Margaret?

494
00:59:34.166 --> 00:59:36.333
You might could start
with the dance tonight.

495
00:59:37.541 --> 00:59:42.000
Take it from me, you don't want people
speculating the way they have been.

496
00:59:42.083 --> 00:59:44.083
You might want to show 'em you're okay.

497
00:59:45.458 --> 00:59:46.458
Oh, you're right.

498
00:59:47.500 --> 00:59:49.750
We really should get out more.

499
00:59:49.833 --> 00:59:50.958
Yeah.

500
01:00:01.000 --> 01:00:02.708
We're really going to the dance?

501
01:00:02.791 --> 01:00:05.791
Esther said
people were worried about us, so…

502
01:00:06.666 --> 01:00:09.041
We have to put on a good face and go.

503
01:00:11.666 --> 01:00:13.208
Well, Sheriff Bell will be there.

504
01:00:14.791 --> 01:00:16.916
We could tell him about Wallace,

505
01:00:18.041 --> 01:00:19.666
what's been happening.

506
01:00:22.041 --> 01:00:23.958
Without the letter from your father...

507
01:00:27.000 --> 01:00:30.166
If the sheriff thought
something was wrong, or...

508
01:00:30.250 --> 01:00:36.166
He could take you both.
Promise me you won't mention it.

509
01:00:44.833 --> 01:00:47.416
It's so pretty.

510
01:00:47.500 --> 01:00:50.791
Oh. I think it's the wearer.

511
01:01:00.375 --> 01:01:01.750
Stay inside!

512
01:01:16.250 --> 01:01:19.833
We're very well. You?

513
01:01:27.750 --> 01:01:29.666
Rose!

514
01:01:30.291 --> 01:01:33.666
I can't breathe!

515
01:01:33.750 --> 01:01:35.291
Mom!

516
01:01:36.625 --> 01:01:39.208
Mommy! Mom, stop!

517
01:01:39.291 --> 01:01:40.875
What is wrong with you?

518
01:01:43.833 --> 01:01:48.041
You were crying out!
You were choking! You couldn't breathe!

519
01:01:48.125 --> 01:01:49.625
No, I was laughing!

520
01:01:58.958 --> 01:02:00.000
It's ruined.

521
01:02:08.000 --> 01:02:09.833
I don't think we should still go.

522
01:02:12.250 --> 01:02:14.000
You'll still look perfect.

523
01:02:14.750 --> 01:02:16.666
It's not just the dress.

524
01:02:31.916 --> 01:02:33.125
What are you...

525
01:02:33.833 --> 01:02:34.958
Stop!

526
01:02:35.041 --> 01:02:36.458
It's all right, Rose.

527
01:02:38.250 --> 01:02:41.625
Daddy will be home soon,
and we'll sort everything out.

528
01:02:43.875 --> 01:02:47.791
Until then, I just need to go
and show everyone we're okay.

529
01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:18.666
Y'all look right as rain, Margaret.

530
01:03:20.083 --> 01:03:22.750
- We're feeling much better. Thank you.
- Hmm. Mm-hmm.

531
01:03:23.541 --> 01:03:24.541
Excuse me.

532
01:03:27.208 --> 01:03:29.333
- Yeah, that's right.
- Margaret!

533
01:03:32.125 --> 01:03:33.791
Would you, uh, care to go for a spin?

534
01:03:36.875 --> 01:03:37.875
Happy to.

535
01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.500
So, how's things?

536
01:03:47.333 --> 01:03:51.791
Oh, we had a little bug,
but we're feeling much better.

537
01:03:52.416 --> 01:03:55.296
Glad to hear it.
Have you been getting enough rest lately?

538
01:03:58.416 --> 01:03:59.416
Why?

539
01:04:00.583 --> 01:04:02.125
What did Rose say?

540
01:04:02.208 --> 01:04:03.208
What do you mean?

541
01:04:04.541 --> 01:04:08.208
Oh, nothing.
She... She's been having nightmares lately.

542
01:04:08.291 --> 01:04:09.291
Oh.

543
01:04:19.708 --> 01:04:21.250
- Margaret.
- What?

544
01:04:21.333 --> 01:04:23.000
You, uh...

545
01:04:29.250 --> 01:04:30.250
You...

546
01:04:34.541 --> 01:04:36.791
Oh, goodness.

547
01:04:38.166 --> 01:04:40.666
It's just a cut.

548
01:04:41.333 --> 01:04:42.875
It's just my leg.

549
01:04:43.708 --> 01:04:45.208
Please keep playing.

550
01:04:52.375 --> 01:04:54.541
Sorry. Pardon me.

551
01:05:07.333 --> 01:05:09.041
What are you doing with him?

552
01:05:11.083 --> 01:05:14.291
With Reverend Shaw?

553
01:05:19.458 --> 01:05:20.916
Excuse me.

554
01:05:22.125 --> 01:05:24.333
I didn't want the girls to miss the dance,

555
01:05:25.166 --> 01:05:27.916
but this cut
h-has me a little light-headed.

556
01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:29.000
Margaret.

557
01:05:31.500 --> 01:05:35.750
Why don't I stop by later
with that healer that I mentioned?

558
01:05:36.625 --> 01:05:37.708
Healer?

559
01:05:37.791 --> 01:05:38.791
Yeah.

560
01:05:40.166 --> 01:05:41.416
You mean Wallace.

561
01:05:41.500 --> 01:05:42.833
No.

562
01:05:43.458 --> 01:05:45.333
His name is Everett Lee.

563
01:05:46.541 --> 01:05:49.541
He's real nice.
He got me thinking right again and...

564
01:05:50.416 --> 01:05:54.916
He even helps me keep up the house
and he got me this.

565
01:05:58.875 --> 01:06:00.833
I don't care what he's calling himself.

566
01:06:00.916 --> 01:06:04.000
That is the man who was
hiding in our loft, Sheriff.

567
01:06:05.708 --> 01:06:06.916
Who threatened us!

568
01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:08.166
Margaret,

569
01:06:09.166 --> 01:06:10.875
that can't be.

570
01:06:12.208 --> 01:06:14.333
You are housing a murderer.

571
01:06:15.375 --> 01:06:18.916
Henry sent me a letter.
Your healer killed a man at his ca...

572
01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:21.291
No, she... she's telling the truth.

573
01:06:23.125 --> 01:06:27.458
I saw him too.
And... And he threatened to come back.

574
01:06:28.125 --> 01:06:29.125
You see?

575
01:06:30.666 --> 01:06:32.375
He's not of this world.

576
01:06:34.375 --> 01:06:35.375
He's...

577
01:06:37.041 --> 01:06:41.833
He's been sneaking into our house,
moving things at night,

578
01:06:41.916 --> 01:06:44.083
trying to hurt the girls.

579
01:06:45.708 --> 01:06:49.583
He can get through locks, closed windows.

580
01:06:49.666 --> 01:06:51.583
He comes apart like dust.

581
01:06:52.125 --> 01:06:55.833
- He seeps in through the cracks.
- Mom, please. Please, come on.

582
01:06:56.708 --> 01:06:58.166
You can breathe him in.

583
01:06:59.625 --> 01:07:01.750
He'll make you do terrible things.

584
01:07:19.666 --> 01:07:21.875
They're gossiping right about now.

585
01:07:23.666 --> 01:07:25.083
Wondering if I'm...

586
01:07:27.416 --> 01:07:28.416
If I...

587
01:07:28.916 --> 01:07:30.500
But I said I saw him too.

588
01:07:35.208 --> 01:07:36.541
It doesn't matter.

589
01:07:41.416 --> 01:07:43.083
They saw me like this.

590
01:07:54.458 --> 01:07:57.000
Mom?

591
01:08:02.250 --> 01:08:03.791
Mom.

592
01:08:11.916 --> 01:08:12.958
Who did that?

593
01:08:17.583 --> 01:08:18.583
You did.

594
01:08:21.875 --> 01:08:23.583
When?

595
01:08:31.875 --> 01:08:33.083
Was he in me?

596
01:08:45.541 --> 01:08:46.541
It's okay.

597
01:08:50.375 --> 01:08:51.750
Wait, wait.

598
01:08:53.458 --> 01:08:54.750
You heard that, right?

599
01:08:55.500 --> 01:08:56.500
Yes.

600
01:08:57.583 --> 01:08:59.416
But what if it's someone checking on us?

601
01:09:01.666 --> 01:09:05.541
Put your masks on. Slide fabric
under the door the moment I leave.

602
01:09:31.541 --> 01:09:32.661
<i>Margaret.</i>

603
01:09:33.833 --> 01:09:35.291
Wallace!

604
01:09:37.708 --> 01:09:39.791
<i>Margaret.</i>

605
01:09:41.333 --> 01:09:42.500
<i>Here, Margaret.</i>

606
01:09:43.291 --> 01:09:44.375
<i>Margaret.</i>

607
01:09:44.458 --> 01:09:45.818
<i>Here, Margaret.</i>

608
01:09:46.750 --> 01:09:48.166
<i>You'll be just like me.</i>

609
01:09:48.250 --> 01:09:49.791
<i>You'll be just like me.</i>

610
01:09:51.000 --> 01:09:52.000
<i>Margaret.</i>

611
01:09:52.083 --> 01:09:53.963
<i>- Here, Margaret.
- Margaret.</i>

612
01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:56.375
<i>People are talking.</i>

613
01:10:02.291 --> 01:10:03.541
Behind you.

614
01:10:16.750 --> 01:10:17.916
Mom!

615
01:10:19.083 --> 01:10:22.375
What happened? Was it Wallace?

616
01:10:25.291 --> 01:10:26.916
Yes, but he vanished!

617
01:10:29.041 --> 01:10:30.375
What do you mean?

618
01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:35.500
Like the book!

619
01:10:35.583 --> 01:10:38.208
He's in the air, Rose!

620
01:10:39.750 --> 01:10:41.541
He could be anywhere!

621
01:10:44.416 --> 01:10:48.000
Get inside! Now!

622
01:11:49.708 --> 01:11:50.833
Mom?

623
01:11:52.791 --> 01:11:53.875
Wallace?

624
01:12:56.583 --> 01:13:02.125
Ada, I'm sorry.

625
01:13:02.916 --> 01:13:05.916
I'm sorry.

626
01:13:06.416 --> 01:13:08.750
Please, let me in.

627
01:13:08.833 --> 01:13:11.750
Please.

628
01:13:11.833 --> 01:13:13.416
Please.

629
01:13:13.500 --> 01:13:17.166
- Mom?
- I'm sorry.

630
01:13:17.250 --> 01:13:18.750
I'm so sorry.

631
01:13:52.333 --> 01:13:54.541
Mom?

632
01:14:01.208 --> 01:14:02.666
You're asleep.

633
01:14:04.291 --> 01:14:05.708
It's you.

634
01:14:06.791 --> 01:14:08.750
You're sleepwalking again.

635
01:14:11.250 --> 01:14:12.083
It's me.

636
01:14:12.166 --> 01:14:14.333
It's Rose.

637
01:14:17.208 --> 01:14:19.958
Mom, it's me! Wake up.

638
01:14:20.541 --> 01:14:22.642
- Don't shoot, it's Rose!
<i>- Don't shoot, it's Rose!</i>

639
01:14:22.666 --> 01:14:24.416
- It's your daughter!
<i>- It's your daughter!</i>

640
01:14:25.375 --> 01:14:27.333
Don't shoot.

641
01:14:27.416 --> 01:14:28.936
- Put the gun down.
<i>- Put the gun down.</i>

642
01:14:29.791 --> 01:14:32.309
- Mommy, I'm really scared.
<i>- Mommy, I'm really scared.</i>

643
01:14:32.333 --> 01:14:33.767
- You have to trust me!
<i>- You have to trust me!</i>

644
01:14:33.791 --> 01:14:35.017
- You have to wake up!
<i>- You have to wake up!</i>

645
01:14:35.041 --> 01:14:36.125
You're not Rose.

646
01:14:36.208 --> 01:14:37.125
Mom.

647
01:14:37.208 --> 01:14:41.958
Mama, Mama, Mama, Mama!

648
01:14:42.041 --> 01:14:44.750
- Mama! Ma...
- Mama!

649
01:14:53.916 --> 01:14:56.041
Rose, what are you doing out here?

650
01:14:57.833 --> 01:15:00.833
The Grey Man isn't haunting us.

651
01:15:01.583 --> 01:15:03.291
What are you talking about?

652
01:15:03.958 --> 01:15:04.958
It's you.

653
01:15:05.458 --> 01:15:07.559
You're
doing things in your sleep again.

654
01:15:07.583 --> 01:15:11.125
That's how the chairs moved
and how the bed caught fire.

655
01:15:20.375 --> 01:15:25.125
You can never say that again
about the sleepwalking.

656
01:15:25.208 --> 01:15:26.208
Not to anyone.

657
01:15:30.083 --> 01:15:31.916
Mom, why are you doing this?

658
01:15:32.875 --> 01:15:33.875
Why?

659
01:15:34.708 --> 01:15:36.333
To protect you.

660
01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:42.125
Then we should have left.

661
01:15:43.166 --> 01:15:45.708
- I was trying to keep us all together.
- Mom.

662
01:15:47.500 --> 01:15:50.500
You, me,

663
01:15:52.250 --> 01:15:53.250
and your sisters.

664
01:15:53.333 --> 01:15:55.250
Ada is dead!

665
01:15:58.208 --> 01:16:00.125
Don't you understand?

666
01:16:01.708 --> 01:16:05.416
You girls are me.

667
01:16:08.166 --> 01:16:09.916
Parts of me.

668
01:16:10.541 --> 01:16:13.541
- Cutaway pieces that never heal.
- Mom, you're scaring me.

669
01:16:15.333 --> 01:16:17.500
I bleed when you're hurt.

670
01:16:18.916 --> 01:16:22.333
I'm alive in that grave…

671
01:16:22.416 --> 01:16:25.416
…suffocating under
the dirt with your sister.

672
01:16:26.541 --> 01:16:28.083
And I would do anything,

673
01:16:28.875 --> 01:16:32.541
anything to keep us together,

674
01:16:33.041 --> 01:16:35.250
to keep us whole.

675
01:16:46.666 --> 01:16:48.500
Rose!

676
01:17:07.708 --> 01:17:08.958
Ollie!

677
01:17:24.583 --> 01:17:27.958
Aunt Esther?

678
01:17:54.708 --> 01:17:56.750
It's too late!

679
01:17:58.500 --> 01:18:01.083
There's nowhere to go, Rose!

680
01:18:02.125 --> 01:18:03.833
Let her go!

681
01:18:03.916 --> 01:18:04.916
Mom!

682
01:18:08.750 --> 01:18:10.750
That wasn't Wallace.

683
01:18:10.833 --> 01:18:12.666
You killed Aunt Esther.

684
01:18:12.750 --> 01:18:14.250
You're hurting her, Rose!

685
01:18:14.333 --> 01:18:16.416
Let her go!

686
01:18:16.500 --> 01:18:17.500
Help!

687
01:18:21.958 --> 01:18:23.250
They will take you.

688
01:18:23.333 --> 01:18:25.375
They will take you away. Please.

689
01:18:53.416 --> 01:18:54.833
Hi, sweet pea.

690
01:18:54.916 --> 01:18:56.000
Where's Mama?

691
01:19:15.875 --> 01:19:18.000
Rose, you all right?

692
01:19:22.791 --> 01:19:24.416
She's not fit.

693
01:19:25.166 --> 01:19:26.416
Rose.

694
01:19:29.666 --> 01:19:30.875
All right now.

695
01:19:31.666 --> 01:19:33.333
You two just go wait in there.

696
01:19:38.583 --> 01:19:39.791
Don't worry.

697
01:19:39.875 --> 01:19:42.083
We're just gonna have
a nice little chat, all right?

698
01:19:45.625 --> 01:19:48.458
I don't know what's gotten into her.

699
01:19:50.666 --> 01:19:52.333
For the coyotes.

700
01:19:55.541 --> 01:19:56.916
Had one recently?

701
01:19:58.458 --> 01:20:00.083
They're always around.

702
01:20:09.500 --> 01:20:13.250
Did, uh, did...
Did Esther come by, Margaret?

703
01:20:13.333 --> 01:20:16.125
She-She said she was gonna check in.

704
01:20:16.208 --> 01:20:18.958
I hope she wasn't lost in the storm.

705
01:20:22.791 --> 01:20:25.333
Margaret, the-the girls seem rattled.

706
01:20:28.541 --> 01:20:30.583
Stir crazy, I guess.

707
01:20:34.333 --> 01:20:35.791
Maybe I ought to take 'em.

708
01:20:37.458 --> 01:20:39.458
Just till Henry gets back.

709
01:20:44.916 --> 01:20:46.625
Hey, now, hey.

710
01:20:47.125 --> 01:20:48.458
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

711
01:20:48.541 --> 01:20:50.291
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

712
01:20:51.333 --> 01:20:52.458
Hey, hey, hey.

713
01:20:52.541 --> 01:20:56.000
Margaret, it's just a few days now,
just a few days.

714
01:20:56.083 --> 01:20:58.458
You done good. You done real good.

715
01:22:16.125 --> 01:22:18.750
They're going to hang me, Rose.

716
01:22:21.500 --> 01:22:23.833
But there is a way around it,

717
01:22:24.958 --> 01:22:27.375
a way to stay together.

718
01:22:29.125 --> 01:22:32.291
A reunion that lasts an eternity.

719
01:22:35.458 --> 01:22:39.875
We just go to sleep like any other night,

720
01:22:39.958 --> 01:22:42.666
but longer.

721
01:22:43.875 --> 01:22:45.666
Please, no.

722
01:22:50.708 --> 01:22:52.166
Yes, baby.

723
01:22:54.625 --> 01:22:56.166
It's the only way.

724
01:22:59.416 --> 01:23:01.583
It's okay to be scared.

725
01:23:02.333 --> 01:23:04.125
It's okay. Come here.

726
01:23:05.041 --> 01:23:06.125
Come here.

727
01:23:14.083 --> 01:23:15.250
Oh.

728
01:23:22.041 --> 01:23:23.125
I'm sorry.

729
01:23:25.458 --> 01:23:28.708
I'm so sorry for everything, Rose.

730
01:23:28.791 --> 01:23:32.791
You're the loves of my life,
you know that.

731
01:23:54.791 --> 01:23:58.166
I'm just so tired, Mommy.

732
01:23:58.250 --> 01:24:00.833
Let's go be with Ada. All right?

733
01:24:27.875 --> 01:24:30.250
Can you tell us about the wheat first?

734
01:24:32.750 --> 01:24:33.916
Yes.

735
01:24:41.166 --> 01:24:44.666
Our first year, it just took hold.

736
01:24:45.208 --> 01:24:48.375
The field was-was chest-high.

737
01:24:49.125 --> 01:24:55.375
And when the wind blew, the wheat
would ripple and wave like the ocean.

738
01:24:55.458 --> 01:25:00.375
And we'd play in that field for hours.

739
01:25:01.125 --> 01:25:02.416
All together.

740
01:25:03.750 --> 01:25:06.666
Could we have the medicine
in some peaches?

741
01:25:11.875 --> 01:25:14.291
I think that's a wonderful idea.

742
01:25:39.875 --> 01:25:40.875
Ollie!

743
01:25:42.708 --> 01:25:43.708
Mom!

744
01:25:45.333 --> 01:25:48.041
I-I tried to stop her,
but Ollie got scared and ran out.

745
01:25:48.125 --> 01:25:50.916
She has to be with us.

746
01:25:51.708 --> 01:25:53.166
She could be drowning!

747
01:26:00.125 --> 01:26:03.583
Oh, please!

748
01:26:04.333 --> 01:26:06.166
Where is she?

749
01:27:02.583 --> 01:27:04.333
I'm sorry.
